# Findings: see, do not swallow (hard rule)

Operator goal (Phil, 2026-08-29): **reduce the burden on auditors and IT
to see what needs to be fixed. We do not have to fix everything that we
find.**

## The rule

> **Workstation Assurance (WA) and Current State Compliance (CSC) exist
> so auditors and IT can see what needs action. Detect is not remediate.
> Customer-supplied controls are flagged and retested. Never imply AIC
> remediates every finding. Never add Fix-It for antivirus, host
> firewall, or disk encryption.**

## Required

- Surface Needs IT / Product can repair / Observe only on existing CSC
  and WA finding rows (`action_owner`). Do not invent a second queue.
- Fix-It apply only where a Live repair path already exists.
- Auditor words: Live / Partial / Absent / BLOCKED. Never Met /
  certified for the Organization Seeking Assessment (OSA).
- US English. No lab leaks. Expand WA / CSC on first use.

## Forbidden

- Fix-It apply on detect-only / `flag_for_it` / `customer_supplied_control`
  rows
- Claiming we fix everything we find
- Met / certified / assessment-ready for the OSA

